 fundraising and a July D-sponsored poll showing a one-point race", "Thin, dated polling (one usable poll, 67 days old) keeps uncertainty high"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a narrow Republican edge: an R+5 seat with an incumbent, offset by a favorable Democratic environment and Killin's fundraising advantage. Raters cluster at Lean R and markets price Crank near 69%, so a modest Republican margin of about three points fits the evidence better than a pure tossup.", "watch": "Any fresh independent polling or a shift in the national environment could move this back toward a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 67 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Jeff Crank (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Colorado's 5th District, anchored in Colorado Springs, leans Republican by about five points, but first-term incumbent Jeff Crank faces a well-funded challenge from Democrat Jessica Killin, who has actually out-raised him. The national political environment favors Democrats this cycle, and a July poll from a Democratic firm showed the race essentially tied, drawing attention to a district that has never elected a Democrat.\n\nStill, most professional raters place the race in Lean Republican territory, and prediction markets give Crank roughly a two-in-three chance. With only one recent poll available and dueling attack ads dominating the airwaves, uncertainty is high, but the weight of evidence points to a narrow Crank advantage.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.332, "margin": -2.57}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3239, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3532, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.346, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2907, "margin": -3.0}]}